# The Quiet Archive - EP11 Victorian London in the Fog (a November evening, around the year 1880)
# Structure: for the first time the listener has a small role - a clerk leaving an office near the Strand at the end of the
#   working day and walking home through the fog, slowly, to a rented room in a quiet square. The quarter chimes of the
#   great clock at Westminster, heard muffled through the fog, are the thread: each chapter begins a little later in the
#   evening. Order: the office door -> the river wall -> the lamplighter -> the cab shelter -> the street sellers ->
#   the square -> the parlour fire -> bed.
# New scenes: "fogstreet" = a terrace of brick houses in deep yellow fog: sash windows, fanlights over the doors, area
#   railings, chimney pots smoking, a red pillar box, a plane tree, gas lamps whose light becomes great soft halos
#   (_halos), and the lamplighter walking along with his long pole, its little flame bobbing at the tip (_lamplighter).
# "embankment" = the river wall at night: granite parapet with lion-head mooring rings, dolphin lamp standards
#   receding in the fog, the obelisk of Cleopatra's Needle, the clock tower with its lit dial far off, the arches of a
#   bridge, lamplight trembling on the water (_wlights) and a steam tug with a lit wheelhouse crossing slowly (_tug).
# "cabstand" = a cab rank by a green cabmen's shelter (lit windows, stove pipe smoking), a hansom cab with its lamps lit
#   and a horse in a rug who nods and breathes out little clouds of steam (_hansom), a chestnut seller's brazier glowing.
# "parlour" = a rented first-floor parlour: coal fire in a cast-iron grate (fires), mantel with a clock under a glass
#   dome, a wall clock whose pendulum swings (_pendulum), gas bracket with glass shade, armchair with antimacassar,
#   aspidistra, kettle steam on the hob, the window with lace curtains and the fog pressing on the glass, a street lamp
#   halo beyond it; a cat asleep on the hearthrug.
# New "drizzle" particles (fine wet fog drops drifting down and catching the gaslight); palette keys "fog" and "gas".
